+# Full backend deployment — 2026-10-18
+
+The owner explicitly requested deployment of the full backend after the player inspection/grants implementation. FB18A includes the complete backend and Studio UI, cloud API/worker/all five existing owned job definitions and the existing PC API/worker. FB18B includes the actual matching compiler27 / physics0.66 / rules23 verifier. FB18C preserves existing accounts, purchases, Coins, achievements, track documents, historical revisions and records, with fresh backups and before/after fingerprints. FB18D verifies the new player inventory/grant picker through read-only live browser checks; no live account grant or charge is requested or performed.
+
+## Release and current execution
+
+The retained cloud service was healthy at schema42 with an empty verification queue and one available worker. Every owned cloud runtime target used the previous complete image `8707116d7acaf1a8ced96d231402eccc3a461742ccb1274bcc1260b923f55c4c`. All five job definitions, including the historical manual `pace2` job, were inventoried. PC container identities and private configuration were captured before changes.
+
+The source snapshot contains the entire current Python backend and stripped canonical verification inputs. Package proof records 199 backend files and 140 canonical files, with 14 changed backend files and five changed canonical files relative to the previous image. The new grant API, track link route, all existing routes and schema42 are checked during image construction. The exact existing dependency lock and pinned Godot4.7.2 are retained; the image builds offline from the existing complete image.
+
+The candidate image is `sha256:303c521ef4469697dc164daa560e661de2c0509c2494b6b83717c1a661517e2e`. Its actual native manifest advertises compiler27, physics0.66 and rules23. Native import, the unchanged five-lap oval input/timing golden and its ten-second rewind pass. The packaged golden advances its expected rule version from22 to23; no recorded inputs, timing or rewind assertions are relaxed. Public document byte hashes and fresh native rules23 validation pass for all28 existing public heads before cloud writes.
+
+The PC plan uses the same candidate image and immutable source bind. Original BMT environment values are retained per service, and the existing object volume mapping is checked before stopping either service. Original database/object volumes, credentials and runtime settings are retained. Cloud updates keep existing environment, IAM, limits, providers, notifications and scheduler definitions; no new recurring monitoring or external integration is activated.
+
+## Actual commands and evidence
+
+The dated tools retain the established guarded deployment logic while using separate18 October work directories and receipts. Each stage operates on captured owned resources and checks the expected image/configuration before mutation.
+
+```powershell
+& .tools/backend-venv/Scripts/python.exe -X utf8 .tools/full_backend_deploy_20261018.py <stage>
+& .tools/backend-venv/Scripts/python.exe -X utf8 .tools/full_backend_validate_catalog_20261018.py
+& .tools/backend-venv/Scripts/python.exe -X utf8 .tools/full_backend_pc_20261018.py <stage>
+& .tools/backend-venv/Scripts/python.exe -X utf8 .tools/full_backend_pc_plan_20261018.py
+```
+
+Actual cloud stages: inspect, extract, freeze, prepare, build, test, recheck, push, backup, preview, maintenance, snapshot, migrate, snapshot-migration, catalog, canary, promote, smoke, catalog-http, browser, finish. PC stages: prepare, backup, snapshot, migrate, preview, catalog, promote, verify. The PC settings/volume plan check follows prepare. Mutating stages sharing a receipt run sequentially. The `recheck` and `snapshot-migration` stages resolve the specific setup issues below.
+
+Evidence lives in [the release evidence directory](evidence/full-backend-deploy-2026-10-18/). Private full resource descriptions, configuration, errors and PC SQL/object backups remain under the ignored `build/full-backend-deploy-2026-10-18/` directory. Public receipts include the initial inventory, frozen source hashes, package proof, actual candidate manifest, offline catalogue validation, exact-image test results, backups, data comparisons and final runtime/browser verification as those stages complete. This document does not imply an unfinished stage passed; final rollout receipts determine completion.
+
+## Initial setup corrections and scope
+
+The sandbox's first WSL probe returned access denied; the authorized deployment uses reviewed elevated access to the existing Docker daemon and cloud CLI. Source preparation initially found generated Python bytecode in the frozen deployment-tool directory. One generated `.pyc` was removed from that owned snapshot, preserving exact source hashes and all acceptance assertions; preparation then passed. The shared source later moved the existing track-links import into the main import block; the validated frozen image already contains the identical module and route. Concurrent editor catalogue filtering changes are not consumed by the server verifier. Every catalogue constant/function and asset definition actually consumed by canonical scripts is byte-exact. [Source comparison](evidence/full-backend-deploy-2026-10-18/frozen-source-current-comparison.json) records these reviewed differences without modifying the validated image.
+
+The first exact-image gate reports **483 passed, one failed, 12 skipped** in675.00 seconds. The failure is the historical-board preservation test's explicit rules22 fixture assertion: the harness had copied the packaged rules23 acceptance golden over that historical test fixture. Only the test fixture is restored to its original rules22 metadata; the packaged native golden remains rules23. The runtime image, recorded inputs/timing and all assertions are unchanged. The affected verifier/trajectory/hairpin recheck passes **78 tests, two skips** in127.72 seconds. The separate Windows client HTTP-adapter test passes in5.23 seconds. [Initial gate](evidence/full-backend-deploy-2026-10-18/exact-image-tests-initial.log), [fixture correction](evidence/full-backend-deploy-2026-10-18/gate-test-fixture-adjustments.json), [recheck](evidence/full-backend-deploy-2026-10-18/exact-image-recheck.log) and [Windows adapter](evidence/full-backend-deploy-2026-10-18/windows-client-adapter.log) retain actual outcomes. This is not a pristine complete-suite pass or a full artificial-driver calibration claim.
+
+The migration completes before its first data-comparison attempt reaches a local command-length guard. Its compressed baseline is7472 base64 characters, above the retained7400-character boot limit. LZMA reduces the same exact comparison program/baseline to7052 characters. LZMA is verified in the exact image; the unchanged comparison then passes through a dedicated resume stage. No fingerprint, column, table or command-length assertion is removed. A local transport probe first used an incorrect image tag, failed without running a container, and was rerun against the receipt's actual image tag.
+
+The first live browser run stops on its sample-population assertion before browser navigation: the rolling window had advanced a UTC day and excluded11 older accounts, returning589 active players. Extending that verification window by one day includes the complete retained sample history and preserves the original600-player assertion. Final66 views pass with zero JavaScript errors, failed admin reads or write requests. The initial output is retained in `browser-run-initial.log`. Neither correction changes live player data.
+
+The grant implementation's earlier configured PostgreSQL service at localhost:55439 remains separate from this release harness. Release tests use a fresh owned internal-network PostgreSQL container. No live player database is used for tests. The release includes all current backend behavior; it does not build or install a game client. Older phone builds still require a matching client update. No phone attachment check, APK/export/install or physical-device test is performed.
+
+## Completion
+
+Cloud API **bmt-stg-e7a444ab-api-00086-vud**, its one matching worker and **all five existing owned job definitions** now use `europe-west1-docker.pkg.dev/beat-my-track/bmt-stg-e7a444ab-images/backend@sha256:303c521ef4469697dc164daa560e661de2c0509c2494b6b83717c1a661517e2e`. The existing PC API/worker use the identical image and frozen source. Both advertise actual compiler27 / physics0.66 / rules23 on Godot4.7.2; schema remains42. Cloud writes are reopened, the original worker count is restored and temporary tags/update lock are removed. The historical manual `pace2` job receives the image without being rerun.
+
+Managed SQL backup **1792347222167** succeeds. The PC's complete quiesced `database.dump`, `objects.tar`, SHA256 manifest and COMPLETE marker remain private under the owned build directory. All56 selected cloud semantic fingerprints and **all99 original PC table fingerprints** are exact across migration and catalogue insertion. The original PC15 players,190 runs and181 versions remain;27 new versions bring that version count to208. Cache-row comparisons retain every original version's entries while allowing entries for the newly inserted revisions. The cloud appends28 matching revisions. Original documents and records are retained; old results are not converted into new-rules scores.
+
+The cloud native/schema/storage smoke succeeds. Cloud and PC each report one ready matching worker, authenticated grant-route availability and all19 Studio assets matching the release bytes. Read-only HTTP verification checks all28 public heads/documents, their immediately prior links and both earlier saved links for each of27 official tracks. No live player grant or real charge is performed.
+
+Real Edge passes **66 read-only view checks** at1440px and390px, including the selected-player inventory and searchable grant picker. Full retained-window activity remains600 players; the recent window has359. There are zero captured JavaScript errors, failed admin reads, write requests or global horizontal overflows. The picker excludes already-owned kits according to the authoritative inventory. [Desktop picker](evidence/full-backend-deploy-2026-10-18/grant-picker-1440.png), [390px picker](evidence/full-backend-deploy-2026-10-18/grant-picker-390.png) and [browser receipt](evidence/full-backend-deploy-2026-10-18/populated-browser.json) show the actual deployed UI.
+
+[Completion receipt](evidence/full-backend-deploy-2026-10-18/completion.json), cloud/PC rollout receipts and before/after comparisons retain the evidence. `tools/` contains audit copies of the actual dated operational scripts; their operational entry points remain under `.tools/`. A source-only `task-only.patch` and SHA256 checkpoint preserve these documentation/tool changes without committing unrelated shared work.
+
+The tool is available at **Studio → Player support → Player directory → selected player → Purchases & grants**. Refresh an already-open Studio tab to load the new assets. Owner workflow/driving acceptance, a matching game-client update for older phone builds, separate artificial-driver calibration and production load/restore exercises remain outside these checks. No phone attachment check, physical-device test or APK action is performed.
